`,u.jsx(a.p,{children:"With the automotive industry shifting towards Zonal Architecture, in-vehicle networks have become exponentially complex. However, existing monitoring tools relied heavily on text-based logs, which lacked spatial context."}),`
`,u.jsx(a.p,{children:"Engineers had to mentally map abstract error codes to physical locations, leading to high cognitive load and delayed diagnosis. The disconnection between digital data and physical reality was a major bottleneck in the maintenance workflow."}),`
